From 2ddd97472e02295a1b9013caaf16cb827e3de4b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael John <mj@tierone.software>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:51:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] patch: handle savestr() NULL in fetchname()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

savestr() returns NULL (setting out_of_mem) rather than exiting when
using_plan_a is set, and plan A is in effect during all fetchname()
calls (patch-header parsing).  The result was strchr()'d and stat()'d
unchecked — a crash-only DoS when memory pressure lands on a patch
parse (attacker-influenced via a huge hostile patch under rlimits).
Propagate NULL; every caller already handles it (the plan-A retry in
patch.c still engages via out_of_mem).

Present verbatim in freebsd-src main (usr.bin/patch).
Upstream patch queued as upstream-patches/0054.
---
 src.freebsd/patch/util.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src.freebsd/patch/util.c b/src.freebsd/patch/util.c
index 17e652836..aca1b13bd 100644
--- a/src.freebsd/patch/util.c
+++ b/src.freebsd/patch/util.c
@@ -370,6 +370,8 @@ fetchname(const char *at, bool *exists, int strip_leading)
 		return NULL;
 	}
 	name = fullname = t = savestr(at);
+	if (t == NULL)
+		return NULL;
 
 	tab = strchr(t, '\t') != NULL;
 	/* Strip off up to `strip_leading' path components and NUL terminate. */
@@ -395,6 +397,8 @@ fetchname(const char *at, bool *exists, int strip_leading)
 	}
 	name = savestr(name);
 	free(fullname);
+	if (name == NULL)
+		return NULL;
 
 	*exists = stat(name, &filestat) == 0;
 	return name;
